{"name":"Red Rooster","hex":"#7e5146","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"rooster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male domestic chicken (Gallus gallus domesticus) or other gallinaceous bird.","A bird or bat which roosts or is roosting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rooster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Rooster","blocks":[{"text":"Red Rooster is an Australian fast food chain. It sells roast chicken alongside common fast food items, such as burgers, chips, salads, and beverages. Since 2021, it has also offered fried chicken."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Red_Rooster_Logo.png/330px-Red_Rooster_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Rooster","wikidata":"Q376466"},{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken","wikidata":"Q780"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/REROWG0011_Shot1_1080x1080_v1.png/500px-REROWG0011_Shot1_1080x1080_v1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/REROWG0011_Shot1_1080x1080_v1.png/500px-REROWG0011_Shot1_1080x1080_v1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red Rooster Fried Chicken","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AREROWG0011_Shot1_1080x1080_v1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chick